  "notes": "Antibody design focuses on binding loops within a framework and a chosen molecular format. RFantibody combines computational design with experimental screening and characterization. RFD4-Proteina documents antibody CDR design as a supported task. TAP flags unusual calculated properties relative to clinical-stage antibodies, providing an early developability screen. Affinity optimization, format choice and functional evaluation continue after the first binder. The diagram is conceptual and does not depict a molecular structure or an experimental result.\n\nSources\n[RFANTIBODY] Bennett et al. Atomically accurate de novo design of antibodies with RFdiffusion. Nature 649, 183–193 (2026), online 5 November 2025\nhttps://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-025-09721-5\nhttps://github.com/RosettaCommons/RFantibody\n\n[RFD4] NVIDIA and Baker Laboratory. RFD4-Proteina documentation and model card\nhttps://docs.nvidia.com/nim/bionemo/rfd4-proteina/overview\nhttps://huggingface.co/nvidia/RFD4-Proteina-Diffusers\n\n[TAP] Raybould et al. Five computational developability guidelines for therapeutic antibody profiling. PNAS (2019)\nhttps://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.1810576116\nhttps://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC6410772/\n\nSource check: 8 November 2026. Representative tools, not an exhaustive ranking."
